  "reason": "The current best is config_018 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) at 0.7207. The evidence strongly favors: (1) imagenet_vit_l over resnet50 (~8.4% gain), (2) scvi_n200 over scgpt (~21% gain), and (3) transformer over avgpool (small but consistent gain). The only untested dimension on this best-known backbone is the fusion method (concat vs. weighted). config_044 tests weighted fusion with the exact same encoders and aggregation as config_018, directly exploiting the strongest evidence while resolving the remaining uncertainty about whether learned modality weighting can push accuracy above 0.72. With 5 experiments left, this is the highest-information, lowest-risk next step: if weighted fusion helps, it confirms a direction for further refinement; if not, we can pivot to exploring pca_n2000 or singleprofile variants with the remaining budget."
}

